*_cache*
# ...but that glob is for cache DATA, not for source that happens to say
# "cache". `scripts/warm_cache.py` was silently not added by `git add` on
# 2026-10-22, while docs/design/architecture.md had already been committed
# citing it -- so a clone would have had a doc naming a file that was not
# there, and test_doc_citations would have failed for everyone but the author.
!scripts/warm_cache.py
*_files*
*.bak
*.sav*
*.tex
*.idx
*.tmp

# data directory
private_data*
private_data/*

# generated caches; data/manifest.json stays tracked
data/cache/

# Vendor downloads never belong in the tree -- they go to ~/dl/databento/ and
# are uploaded to R2 from there. `ext/` does not exist; this is a guard for the
# habit, because a couple of GiB of tick data plus one `git add -A` is not
# something you undo quickly. See docs/setup/R2_ACCESS.md section 7.
ext/

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Quarto / HTML output
*.html

node_modules/*

